# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallbacks for the combined monorepo build.
# Real files (assets, index.html) are served first; these only catch client-side routes.
#
# The Sang app site (react-router / BrowserRouter) lives under /app. Two Cloudflare
# gotchas shape these rules:
#   1. A wildcard `/app/*  /app/index.html  200` is rejected as an infinite-loop redirect.
#   2. A rewrite whose destination ends in `/index.html` gets auto-normalized to a 308
#      redirect to the directory, which changes the URL and breaks the client route.
# So we rewrite each /app route to the DIRECTORY `/app/` (already normalized -> served
# as index.html with a 200, URL preserved, so react-router renders the right route).
# Add a line here whenever the Sang site gains a new route.
/app/privacy   /app/   200
#
# The CMS at / is hash-routed, so this standard root SPA fallback covers it.
/*             /index.html   200
